{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"soured-elmy-ostrich","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Context\n\nParent epic `a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb`. S1 (`248f-ac00-18db-4259`) adds the peer-confirmation store\nand writes records when WE push a link. This story adds the second, independent evidence source:\na link observed in an authoritative remote snapshot is peer-confirmed even if this clone never\npushed it (peer-created links, links pushed before the store existed, links pushed by another\nclone).\n\nThe epic's binding constraint: **a partial / paginated / failed / stale read is NON-EVIDENCE** —\nit can neither confirm nor deny. rebar already has exactly this completeness signal and this\nstory must consume it rather than invent one:\n`fetcher.py::merge_issuelinks_map` writes the per-issue `issuelinks` key ONLY on an authoritative\nread — an absent key means UNOBSERVED (truncated page walk, HTTP 410, failed enrichment, backend\nwithout `get_issuelinks_map`), while `[]` means authoritatively-empty. This is the same G1 signal\nthe inbound removal differ already depends on. `BackendPaginationStallError` re-raises rather\nthan degrading, so a stalled pager never reaches this code as a \"complete\" read.\n\nThere is no snapshot revision counter in the codebase; `pass_id` is the only handle (epic comment\nD3), so records store `confirmed_pass`, not an ordered revision. Do not build ordering logic on it.\n\n# Scope\n\n- `peer_confirmations.py`: add `confirm_from_snapshot(store, curr_snapshot, binding_store, local_tickets, pass_id)`.\n  For each snapshot entry that HAS the `issuelinks` key (authoritative), map observed peer links\n  into LOCAL relation vocabulary with the existing `link_direction` helpers (`observed_peer_deps`),\n  resolve peer keys to local ids via the binding store, and record each as\n  `direction=\"snapshot\"`, `source=\"snapshot\"`, carrying the vendor link id when present.\n  Entries WITHOUT the `issuelinks` key are skipped entirely — no record, no negative record.\n- `reconcile.py`: call it from the persist phase as a sibling of the existing\n  `_advance_baselines(binding_store, ctx.curr_snapshot, ...)` call, then save the store. Failure\n  to confirm must never abort the pass (log and continue), matching `_advance_baselines`.\n- Confirmation is monotonic and additive in this story: observing a link confirms it; NOT\n  observing it never un-confirms. Un-confirmation is deliberately excluded — it would reintroduce\n  \"absence is evidence\", the exact failure the epic forbids.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 A snapshot entry with `issuelinks` present and a matching bound link produces a record\n      with `direction=\"snapshot\"`, `source=\"snapshot\"`, and the current `pass_id`.\n- [ ] AC2 A snapshot entry with the `issuelinks` key ABSENT produces no record for that issue,\n      even when the link is present in the local graph and managed.\n- [ ] AC3 An authoritative `issuelinks: []` produces no record and does NOT remove or invalidate\n      an existing confirmation (no un-confirmation path exists).\n- [ ] AC4 A link whose peer key is unbound in the binding store is skipped (no record, no raise).\n- [ ] AC5 Relation mapping goes through `link_direction`, so an inward vendor link is recorded\n      under the local relation it reads as — asserted for a `Blocks`/`depends_on` inward pair.\n- [ ] AC6 An exception raised inside snapshot confirmation is logged and the reconcile pass still\n      completes and persists (assert via an injected raising store).\n- [ ] AC7 Every touched module stays under the 800-line cap (verify against `git archive HEAD`);\n      `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; new tests pass.\n\n# Out of scope\n\nThe removal decline (S3) and the upgrade backfill (S4). No un-confirmation. No new fetch call —\nthis story consumes `ctx.curr_snapshot` as already fetched.","id":"83d3-61d9-fc59-424b","parent_id":"a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Confirm links from authoritative fetched snapshots"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786558471405692001,"uuid":"ab80febf-6e14-498a-8322-21d64b4f8b20"}